{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalGraphRealization","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalGraphRealization","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalGraphRealization.canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalGraphRealization.canonical","kind":"def","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CrystalGraphRealization.lean#L93-L129","doc":"**The degenerate model** — a `def`, deliberately NOT an `instance`.\n\nBoth carrier types collapse to `PUnit` and both crystal operators return\n`none`, so `crystal_realises` closes by `rfl`: it holds because there is\nnothing for it to say, not because the crystal structure was constructed.\n\nIt was declared `instance` and documented as *\"Faithful instance. Carries the\nexplicit research-grade conjecture as a sorry.\"* Neither half held. There is no\n`sorry` term anywhere in this file — the two occurrences of the word are both in\ndocstrings — so `#print axioms` on anything downstream reported no `sorryAx`,\nand `nodeOf_isHighestWeight` above read as an established result about GS normal\nforms whose only model in scope has exactly one normal form and one node.\n\nAs an `instance` it satisfied every `[CrystalGraphRealization R q]` binder by\nsynthesis. Demoting it changes nothing else: measured 2026-08-24, all twelve\nfiles that bind this class — eight library modules and four content-block\nsiblings — build with **zero** errors afterwards, because every one of those\nbinders is a hypothesis in a signature (the honest §3b-cond shape) rather than a\nsynthesis site. The measurement is sensitive rather than vacuous: with this\ndeclaration a `def`, `inferInstance` for the class fails with *\"failed to\nsynthesize QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalGraphRealization\"*, and succeeds again when it\nis restored to an `instance`.\n\nThe model stays available to anyone who wants it by name; it is simply no longer\nfound by instance synthesis. Same disposition as `triv_hecke` /\n`triv_wedderburn` (PR #5581) and `skeletonRealisation` (PR #5621).\n`QOU/MassEndomorphism/VolumeBridge.lean` is the instance-free design this\nfollows. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalGraphRealization.nodeOf_isHighestWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalGraphRealization.nodeOf_isHighestWeight","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CrystalGraphRealization.lean#L83-L91","doc":"Unconditional packaged form: the crystal node attached to any GS\nnormal form is a Kashiwara highest-weight vector.  This is the\nclean, downstream-usable restatement of `crystal_realises`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalGraphRealization.IsHighestWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalGraphRealization.IsHighestWeight","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CrystalGraphRealization.lean#L74-L81","doc":"Highest-weight predicate on a crystal node: every Kashiwara raising\noperator `ẽ_i` annihilates it.  Standard Kashiwara/Lecouvey\nconvention. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalGraphRealization.nodeOf_highest_weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalGraphRealization.nodeOf_highest_weight","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CrystalGraphRealization.lean#L64-L72","doc":"Unconditional structural lemma: applying any raising operator to\n`nodeOf T` returns `none`, i.e. `nodeOf T` is highest-weight.\nDirect consequence of `crystal_realises`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalGraphRealization.crystal_realises","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalGraphRealization.crystal_realises","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CrystalGraphRealization.lean#L59-L59","doc":"**The conjecture itself**: every GS normal form's crystal node\nis a highest-weight vector.  Plays the role of `sorry`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalGraphRealization.lowering","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalGraphRealization.lowering","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CrystalGraphRealization.lean#L56-L56","doc":"Kashiwara lowering operator `f̃_i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalGraphRealization.raising","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalGraphRealization.raising","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CrystalGraphRealization.lean#L54-L54","doc":"Kashiwara raising operator `ẽ_i` (partial — `none` when applied\nto a highest-weight vector). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalGraphRealization.nodeOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalGraphRealization.nodeOf","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CrystalGraphRealization.lean#L51-L51","doc":"Crystal node attached to a normal form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalGraphRealization.CrystalNode","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalGraphRealization.CrystalNode","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CrystalGraphRealization.lean#L49-L49","doc":"Abstract type of crystal nodes of `Cryst(𝔰𝔩_n)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalGraphRealization.NormalForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalGraphRealization.NormalForm","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CrystalGraphRealization.lean#L47-L47","doc":"Abstract type of Hecke normal forms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalGraphRealization.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalGraphRealization.mk","kind":"ctor","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CrystalGraphRealization.lean#L45-L45","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalGraphRealization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalGraphRealization","kind":"class","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CrystalGraphRealization.lean#L31-L60","doc":"**Crystal-graph realisation (conjecture).**\n\nA normal form `T_w ∈ H_n(R, q)` is realised by a Kashiwara\ncrystal highest-weight vector via the Brundan–Kleshchev\nisomorphism.  The class fields encode:\n- `CrystalNode` — the crystal node type;\n- `nodeOf` — the node attached to a normal form;\n- `raising` / `lowering` — Kashiwara `ẽ_i` and `f̃_i` operators;\n- `crystal_realises` — the conjecture itself: every node attached\n  to a GS normal form is annihilated by every raising operator. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:crystal-graph-realization","label":"conj:crystal-graph-realization","md":"quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/crystal-graph-realization.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}